# Hard-stop paths: changes here never auto-merge. In label mode the pipeline labels such PRs needs-human and
# the owner approves by adding the `human-approved` label; with owner_approval: chat there is no label and the owner
# says "merge" in chat (single GitHub identity, so this file documents ownership rather than enforcing reviews).
# pipeline-setup fills the two placeholders: {{OWNER}} = the repo owner's handle (e.g. @your-login), and the
# {{HARD_STOP_LINES}} line below is replaced by one line per project hard-stop path:  /supabase/migrations/  @your-login
# {{HARD_STOP_LINES}}
/.github/               {{OWNER}}
/.claude/               {{OWNER}}
/scripts/pipeline/      {{OWNER}}
/scripts/verify*        {{OWNER}}
